    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Stretch Transformation Given a Vector and its Image",
    "problem": "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$",
    "worked_solution": "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $v$ and $T(v),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $x$-component of $T(v)$ is $2$ times the $x$-component of $v,$ while\n\n- the $y$-components of $v$ and $T(v)$ are the same.\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $2$ in the $x$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
